...FLOOD ADVISORY IN EFFECT UNTIL 1230 AM CDT SATURDAY...



* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.



* WHERE...A portion of north central Texas, including the following 

  counties, Kaufman and Van Zandt.



* WHEN...Until 1230 AM CDT.



* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas. 



* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...

  - Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Low

    lying and/or poor drainage areas will experience minor

    flooding in the advisory area. Between 2 and 3 inches of rain

    have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are

    forecast.

  - Some locations that will experience flooding include...

    Canton, Myrtle Springs and Wise.





PRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...



Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood 

deaths occur in vehicles.



Be especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the 

dangers of flooding.



