...A SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 745 PM CDT

FOR DICKEY COUNTY...



At 716 PM CDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line

extending from 5 miles north of Oakes to near Ellendale, moving east

at 40 mph.



HAZARD...70 mph wind gusts and nickel size hail.



SOURCE...Radar indicated.



IMPACT...Expect considerable tree damage. Damage is likely to mobile 

         homes, roofs, and outbuildings.



Locations impacted include...

Ellendale, Oakes, Fullerton, Forbes, Ludden, Monango, Guelph, and

Glover.



PRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...



A Tornado Watch remains in effect until 1000 PM CDT for southeastern

North Dakota.



For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a

building.



