Orange FL-Seminole FL-

843 PM EDT Tue Aug 5 2025



...FLOOD ADVISORY NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL 10 PM EDT THIS EVENING...



* WHAT...Urban and small stream flooding caused by excessive 

  rainfall continues.



* WHERE...A portion of east central Florida, including the following 

  counties, Orange and Seminole.



* WHEN...Until 1000 PM EDT.



* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas. 



* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...

  - At 843 PM EDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges

    indicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This is causing

    urban and small stream flooding. Between 2 and 4 inches of

    rain have fallen.

  - Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over

    the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.

  - Some locations that will experience flooding include...

    Orlando, Sanford, Apopka, Altamonte Springs, Oviedo, Winter

    Springs, Winter Park, Casselberry, Maitland, Lake Mary,

    Longwood, Goldenrod, College Park, Lockhart, Azalea Park,

    Pine Hills, Lake Jesup, Conway, Oak Ridge and Belle Isle.

  - http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood



PRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...



Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood 

deaths occur in vehicles.



Be especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the 

dangers of flooding.



&&



